{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he went barefoot (shefi).</b> Its Targum is singular; and it has no parallel." "<b>And the sage</b> Rabbi Abraham, of blessed memory, explained that it is from the language of (Isaiah 41) ״על שפיים״ — 'upon the heights,' which is a high place; its measure would be וילך אל שפי — 'and he went to the height.' And likewise (Numbers 11:35) ״נסעו העם חצרות״ — for he would travel from place to place according to the custom of a diviner, end quote. And the verse alludes to you: even though he was searching after a high place in order to see them gathered in one place and aim his curse at them, even so he found them only scattered to the four winds of the world — and this is the word שפ״י: שְׁפָ־פִּזְרָה יִשְׂרָאֵל — 'Israel is scattered.' And in the Midrash: שפי — he hobbled one leg, but Samson hobbled both legs; it is written here שפי, and it is written there (Genesis 49) שפיפון."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:17.615173790Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}